<title>NETHERLANDS: D.Lloyd sees ABN AMRO 10-15 pct undervalued.</title>
<headline>D.Lloyd sees ABN AMRO 10-15 pct undervalued.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of March 10 research.</p>
<p>Company---------Sector--------Price---Broker----------------</p>
<p>ABN AMRO	  Banking	 138.60  Delta Lloyd Bank</p>
<p>COMMENT: We expect 16.8 pct net profit rise in 1997 with EPS up 14.4 pct. AMRO is 10 to 15 percent undervalued versus Dutch financials, AEX and European peers, based on relative PEs.</p>
<p>    Estimates (NLG):   EPS    pvs EPS   P/E    P/CF   Dividend</p>
<p>    1996 (actual)	9.26    ----     15.0   11.4    4.20</p>
<p>    1997		   10.61   ----     13.1   10.1    4.80</p>
<p>    1998		   11.80   ----     11.7    9.1    5.30</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (Fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
